body:
Reading the frozen header closely, the four DMA functions cannot be implemented as declared, and V40 (VCU_PA_ALLOCATION: "va = guest address via n2vc_dma_guest_map") and V34 (ion_mmap = n2vc_dma_guest_map) are both told to call guest_map.

  int n2vc_dma_guest_map(const struct n2vc_hw *h, struct n2a32_mem *m, uint32_t handle, uint32_t bytes, uint32_t *guest_addr);

The caller has already allocated the handle with h->dma_alloc (which also returned pa), but the prototype takes no pa, n2vc_hw has no handle->pa query, and nothing else in the frozen header reveals it. guest_map therefore cannot fill the "registry of handle, pa, bytes, guest address" the header's comment promises; it can only re-map a handle that some earlier call registered - and that earlier call has the same problem.

Proposed minimal, backward-compatible addition (three declarations after the existing four, no change to them):

  /* V41/V40/V34: the caller knows pa from h->dma_alloc(); map and register it.  Returns 0 or
   * -EINVAL/-ENOMEM/-EEXIST.  The caller keeps the DMA handle: n2vc_dma_guest_unmap() removes the
   * mapping but does not free it. */
  int n2vc_dma_guest_register(const struct n2vc_hw *h, struct n2a32_mem *m, uint32_t handle,
                              uint32_t pa, uint32_t bytes, uint32_t *guest_addr);
  /* Convenience: dma_alloc + register in one call; unmap frees the handle. */
  int n2vc_dma_guest_alloc(const struct n2vc_hw *h, struct n2a32_mem *m, uint32_t bytes,
                           uint32_t flags, uint32_t *handle, uint32_t *pa, uint32_t *guest_addr);
  int n2vc_dma_lookup_handle(uint32_t handle, uint32_t *pa, uint32_t *guest_addr, uint32_t *bytes);

and one sentence in the comment of n2vc_dma_guest_map(): "a handle is mappable this way only after n2vc_dma_guest_register()/n2vc_dma_guest_alloc() registered it; without a pa the map call returns -ENOENT".

Until the header changes I implement exactly that contract in ap/n2vc_dma.c and declare the three additions in ap/n2ap_venc.h (my owned file); guest_map works for registered handles, returns -ENOENT otherwise. Nothing else in the frozen header needs to change. If you prefer a different spelling or to put the additions in include/n2vc_hw.h, say so and I will follow it. Note n2a32_mem has no free(), so guest address space is not reclaimed by unmap either way (documented in my STATUS).
